{
  "version": "formation_structure_v1",
  "policy_version": "formation_policy_v1",
  "description": "Deterministic, versioned, auditable mapping from an exact resolved/projected formation string to (a) a NEUTRAL formation_id token with no semantic loading, and (b) explicit STRUCTURAL attributes (back line / midfield bands / forward line counts) derived from the formation string's own digit-band notation. This is a CONDITIONING KEY + STRUCTURAL DESCRIPTION only, carrying no behavioral assumption (same principle as FORMATION_FAMILY_V1.json). It exists so the Sonnet-facing packet can expose WHAT STRUCTURE a formation represents without exposing the human-readable label itself (V3 patch SS9-12).",
  "authority": "back_line_count and forward_line_count are read literally from the first and last '-'-separated band of the formation string -- this is standard football notation, not an invented convention. When there are exactly two middle bands, the first is labelled holding_midfield_count and the second advanced_midfield_count (deeper-to-more-advanced band order, the conventional reading of e.g. 4-2-3-1); when there is only one middle band, only a combined midfield_count is recorded and the holding/advanced split is left null rather than invented (V3 patch SS10: do not invent structure). Formations with zero or more than two middle bands, or that are otherwise unparseable, get structure_known=false and every count is null -- callers must render this as FORMATION_STRUCTURE_UNKNOWN, never a guessed structure.",
